{
  "id": "semantic_tokens/modifiers/14_control_flow",
  "topic": "semantic_tokens",
  "subtopic": "modifiers",
  "title": "Control flow",
  "summary": "Keywords that transfer control and functions that never return are `controlFlow`",
  "prose": "`if`, `for`, `return` and the other statements that branch, loop or leave\ncarry it, telling them apart from declaration keywords such as `int` or\n`const`. A `[[noreturn]]` function carries it too, as does a macro whose\nexpansion can leave the function.",
  "status": "supported",
  "issues": [],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "main.cpp",
      "text": "[[noreturn]] void fail(const char* reason);\n\nint first_positive(const int* values, int count) {\n    for(int i = 0; i < count; i += 1) {\n        if(values[i] > 0) {\n            return values[i];\n        }\n    }\n    fail(\"none\");\n}\n",
      "markers": []
    }
